#!/usr/bin/env xetal
# __TITLE__: replace this program. Each top-level *.xtl in the game
# directory is run by `just test` (with --seed 1, standard input from
# expected/<name>.in when there is one) and its output compared with
# expected/<name>.out (and .err when it has one).
#
# The rules go in a library beside this file, <Name>.xtl, exporting
# under l: what applies of the game protocol (docs/plan.md A4); this
# program, play.xtl and the page import it with "g:" u_se< "Name":
#   l:n_ew      seed or size -> state
#   l:m_ove     state l:m_ove move -> state
#   l:l_egal    state -> the legal moves
#   l:s_tatus   state -> 0 playing, 1 over or won, 2 lost, 3 draw
#   l:v_iew     state -> a display array
# The state is a flat numeric array, so a page can pass it back in.
'+ r_/ r_ange 10
